  "policies": [
    "Only actual native Kindred components repeat. Ordinary base text, draws, payment and Battlecry quantities are not duplicated merely because their card has Kindred.",
    "A dedicated one-use next_kindred PlayerEffectSpec owns the source. Actual component acceptance captures all source instances, complete prior-owner-turn relation and max2 plan; consumption includes an unsuccessful Kindred condition under explicit local policy pending CN calibration.",
    "Three actual intrinsic Kindred reductions quote complete original source instances, apply the intrinsic operation twice when matched, and consume them once as part of the original payment projection/use receipt. Preview and nonpayment static prices do not consume sources.",
    "Prepared draws/rewards keep their original receiver; triggered sources and additional native bodies accept independently. Same-residence identity, payment, waiting, replay and private boundaries stay public-kernel responsibilities.",
    "Historical community/official-forum user reports are observations only, not CN37 certification. Exact failed-condition consumption, stacked sources, static pricing, repeated Battlecries and alternate-source windows remain M6 policies until calibrated."
  ]
